<div class="col-md-5 pt-0">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-header">
            <h3 class="card-title text-center">Blueprint Import Process</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            Import your blueprints from the Dual Universe MMO (or other external sources) into The Isle! Blueprints must be in JSON format. <br />
            To prepare, you must connect The Isle's server with your account. Follow these steps in order:<br /><br />
            <ol>
                <li>Follow the directions at the MMO's <a target="_blank" href='https://meshexporter.dualuniverse.game/login'>MeshExporter</a> to download the blueprint from the MMO. Use the MeshExporter's "Export" button, not the STL or GLTF buttons.
                <li>Start the MyDualUniverse game, connect to the server "[NA East] The Island", and log in.
                <li>Select the "Site Ops->Link Game Account" within The Isle's website.
                <li>Enter the user name for your MyDU account (case Sensitive) and click search
                <li>Within the MyDU chat window (lower left corner of the game), you'll see a message from the TheIsle bot, with a text token string.
                <li>Enter the token string into the web site's token form field.
                <li>Once linked, other functions within the "Site Ops" menu will become visible. Click on the "Upload Blueprints" option, and select your blueprint.
                <li>Within your nanopack in game, you'll find the blueprint you've uploaded.
                <li>You can now purchase parts from the market or make them in your factory, and deploy your new construct!
            </ol>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>